- Right to counsel: you have the right to hire an attorney; in most civil matters you are not appointed counsel — clarify if any public help is available.
- Right to interpreter: if you need one, request it early — courts usually provide interpreters if requested.
- Self-incrimination: if there are potential criminal implications, confirm how testimony might affect immigration; ask whether invoking the Fifth Amendment applies in your situation.
- Evidence rules & confidentiality: ask about what can be sealed or kept out of public record, and whether settlement terms can be confidential.
- Protective orders: if you fear retaliation or harassment, ask about temporary protective orders and how to request them.
- Record-keeping: ask how to keep records of service, filings, court communications.

