--- AGENT RESPONSE (FULL) ---
Length: 5866 chars
Response (FULL, NOT TRUNCATED):
I can absolutely help you prepare. Below is a focused checklist you can bring to your meeting with Robert Kim plus suggested questions grouped by topic, a short document checklist, what typically happens next in court, and quick prep tips. If you want, I can also draft a concise email or meeting agenda you can send to your lawyer with these questions.

Suggested questions to ask your attorney

A. Case basics & immediate next steps (preliminary hearing)
- What is the exact purpose of the preliminary hearing in this matter? What will the judge decide at that hearing?
- What do you want me to say (or not say) at the preliminary hearing? Do you recommend I attend in person or via phone/zoom?
- What documents or evidence should I bring to the hearing?
- What is the timeline from the preliminary hearing to potential trial (typical scheduling in Maricopa County)?
- Are there steps we can take before the hearing to strengthen our position (motions, evidence preservation, witness prep)?

B. Case strategy & likely outcomes
- What is your recommended strategy for this case right now?
- What are the realistic best-case and worst-case outcomes?
- Are settlement or mediation options available and recommendable? If so, what terms should I consider acceptable?
- What are the strengths and weaknesses of our case and of the ex-spouse’s case?

C. Custody & financial issues
- How do the custody issues interact with this court proceeding? Will this case create, change, or affect temporary custody or parenting time orders?
- Could financial orders (child support, spousal support, division of assets) be issued or affected in this proceeding?
