- Short term (2–6 weeks): attend preliminary hearing; the court may set a schedule (discovery deadlines, settlement conference, pretrial dates) or issue temporary orders.
- Mid term (6–12 weeks): discovery (document exchange, depositions if needed), mediation/settlement talks, pretrial motions (e.g., motions to dismiss, motions in limine).
- Longer term (2–6+ months): trial preparation (witness prep, exhibits, subpoenas), trial, and then post-trial motions or appeals if needed.

