- Discovery/pre-trial: exchange documents, witness lists, possible depositions, motions (to dismiss, for evidence).
- Settlement/mediation: often attempted before trial; sometimes resolves the case.
- Trial (if needed): full presentation of evidence and witnesses; outcome decided by judge.
- Post-trial: possible appeals or enforcement of orders; any immigration follow-ups.

Practical tips
- Organize files (digital & printed) labeled by topic (immigration, housing, custody, finances).
- Make a concise written timeline of events (dates, short descriptions) to give your lawyer.
- Keep copies of everything you send or sign; note dates and names of people you talk to.
- If there’s immediate risk (eviction, removal, child safety), tell your attorney right away.

